#X obj 20 700 outlet~;
#X obj 20 400 e_rec \$0 3200;
#N canvas 200 200 1300 800 play 0;
#X text 20 20 The player \, on only while the loop is heard. One head and no seam: the wrap's jump is part of the waveform \, as a retrigger's is \, and it is raw all the way to the sine \, nothing against aliasing. The rate goes on at the last message's ramp \, 20 ms \, so the knob's places do not zipper. The head goes where the phase says \, less 63 - i for a block's sample i \, as in e_tape (~/Sites/!reference/pure-data.md). It tells the sine how loud it is \, so a silent loop stays silent \, and where it is when asked., f 70;
